#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# array

#% text
# `array(f, n)` gives the list `[f(1), f(2), ..., f(n)]`.

#% text
# `array(f, [n1, n2, ...])` gives nested lists of `f(i1, i2, ...)` with `i1` from 1 to `n1`, `i2` from 1 to `n2`, and so on.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `f` is a function; `table` does the same with an expression and a named variable.

#% item
# The sizes must be non-negative integers.

#% item
# `array(f, n, r)`: indices from the integer `r`, or `n` equally spaced points from `a` to `b` for `r = [a, b]`; for several dimensions a list of such origins. `array(f, dims, r, g)` uses the head `g` instead of `list`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
array(f, 3)
#% output
#= [f(1), f(2), f(3)]

#% cell
array(k => k^2, 5)
#% output
#= [1, 4, 9, 16, 25]

#% cell
array((i, j) => i + j, [2, 3])
#% output
#= [[2, 3, 4], [3, 4, 5]]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Points of a range:

#% cell
array(f, 5, [0, 1])
#% output
#= [f(0), f(1/4), f(1/2), f(3/4), f(1)]

#% text
# Another head:

#% cell
array(c, [2, 2], 1, add)
#% output
#= c(1, 1) + c(1, 2) + c(2, 1) + c(2, 2)

#% text
# A symbolic function gives symbolic entries:

#% cell
array(a, [2, 2])
#% output
#= [[a(1, 1), a(1, 2)], [a(2, 1), a(2, 2)]]

#% text
# Three dimensions:

#% cell
array((i, j, k) => i*j*k, [2, 2, 2])
#% output
#= [[[1, 2], [2, 4]], [[2, 4], [4, 8]]]

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# The Hilbert matrix:

#% cell
array((i, j) => 1/(i + j - 1), [3, 3])
#% output
#= [[1, 1/2, 1/3], [1/2, 1/3, 1/4], [1/3, 1/4, 1/5]]

#% text
# A Vandermonde matrix for interpolation through the points 1, 2, 3:

#% cell
array((i, j) => i^(j - 1), [3, 3])
#% output
#= [[1, 1, 1], [1, 2, 4], [1, 3, 9]]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `table` gives the same with a variable:

#% cell
array(k => 2^k, 6) === table(2^k, k, 6)
#% output
#= true

#% text
# `constant_array` fills with one value:

#% cell
constant_array(0, [2, 3])
#% output
#= [[0, 0, 0], [0, 0, 0]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `table`, `constant_array`, `range`, `identity_matrix`
